{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnot","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":42,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomialCleared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinPolynomialCleared","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L243-L251","doc":"The Skein polynomial `P(q)` (cleared form) as a product of\ntraced volumes.  The actual `P = ∏ V̂_j`, but we compute\n`∏ ((t+t⁻¹)·V̂_j)` to stay integral.\n\nThe power of `(t+t⁻¹)` in the denominator is `A-1`\n(one factor per chain). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.buildChains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.buildChains","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L216-L239","doc":"Build all chain matrices for a nuclear configuration inductively.\n\nWhen nucleon `k` is added:\n1. Each existing chain `M_j` is extended: `M_j ← M_j · T(j, k)`\n2. A new chain `M_{k-1}` is created: `M_{k-1} = T(k-1, k)`\n\nReturns the list of chain matrices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.chainStart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.chainStart","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L213-L214","doc":"The identity 2×2 matrix (start of a new chain). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.extendChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.extendChain","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L209-L211","doc":"Extend a chain matrix by one more crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.crossingMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.crossingMatrix","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L199-L207","doc":"The transfer matrix for a crossing between nucleon types `a` and `b`.\n\nReturns `2 · T` (doubled to stay integral for pn crossings).\nThe factor of 2 is tracked and cancelled in the final Q formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NuclearConfig","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L196-L197","doc":"A nuclear configuration: a list of nucleon types. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolCleared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tracedVolCleared","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L187-L192","doc":"The traced volume `V̂ = z · M[0][0] + M[1][0]` rewritten as\n`(t + t⁻¹) · V̂ = M[0][0] + (t + t⁻¹) · M[1][0]`.\n\nWe work with the **cleared** form to stay in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markov_denom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markov_denom","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L180-L185","doc":"The Markov parameter `z = 1/(t + t⁻¹) = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`.\n\nThis is NOT in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]` — it's in the fraction field.\nFor formal proofs involving `z`, we work with the denominator\n`t + t⁻¹` explicitly and clear it from equations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.two_T_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.two_T_pn","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L169-L176","doc":"Transfer matrix for a proton–neutron crossing.\n`𝔴⁺ = 1`, `𝔴⁰ = −HA/2`.\n\n**Note**: the factor ½ takes us to `ℤ[½][t, t⁻¹]`.\nFor formal proofs, we work with `2·T_pn` to stay integral. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.T_nn","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L164-L167","doc":"Transfer matrix for a neutron–neutron crossing: `T(1, −HA)`.\nFrom the Hecke relation: σ⁻¹ = σ − (q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.T_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.T_pp","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L161-L162","doc":"Transfer matrix for a proton–proton crossing: `T(1, 0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_eq","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L155-L159","doc":"`transferMatrix` unfolds to the matrix literal it always was. Kept as a\n`simp` lemma so proofs that used to `unfold transferMatrix` and land on\n`!![...]` still do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrixOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrixOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L149-L153","doc":"`transferMatrixOf` unfolds to the matrix literal. Marked `simp` because\ndownstream proofs reduce these matrices entry by entry; without it they\nstop at `transferMatrixOf h a b 0 0` and `ring`/`simp` cannot finish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_eq_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_eq_of","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L142-L147","doc":"The symbolic transfer matrix **is** the generic one at the amplitude\n`HA_t` — definitionally, hence `rfl`. This is what makes\n`QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayTransfer.betaTransfer` a second instantiation\nrather than a second definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L130-L140","doc":"The transfer matrix at the symbolic Hecke amplitude `HA_t = q − q⁻¹`.\n\n**Body left as the literal on purpose.** Defining this as\n`transferMatrixOf HA_t c d` typechecks, but seven downstream proofs\n`unfold transferMatrix` and then reduce the `Matrix.cons` normal form\nentry by entry; the extra indirection stops them, and adding\n`transferMatrixOf` to each `unfold` fixed some and not others. The\nrelationship is instead recorded as the `rfl` lemma below, which costs\nno consumer anything and is just as strong. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrixOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrixOf","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L113-L128","doc":"The transfer matrix `T(𝔴⁺, 𝔴⁰)` at a single crossing, over **any**\ncommutative ring, given the Hecke amplitude `h` as data.\n\nT(h; c, d) = ⎡ c·h + d,  c ⎤\n             ⎣ c,        d ⎦\n\n**The amplitude is the parameter, not `q`** (bean `qou-u87j`). The obvious\ngeneralisation — take `q` and form `q - q⁻¹` inside — does not typecheck\nover a `CommRing`: the symbolic ground ring here is\n`R_t = LaurentPolynomial ℤ`, which has no `Inv`, which is precisely why\nthis file carries `t_inv` as a separate element rather than writing `t⁻¹`.\nPassing `h` covers both users: `HA_t` over `ℤ[t,t⁻¹]` below, and\n`q - q⁻¹` over `ℝ` in `QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayTransfer`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TMatrix","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L110-L111","doc":"A 2×2 transfer matrix over `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.w_zero_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.w_zero_t","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L92-L101","doc":"The smoothing amplitude `𝔴⁰(q)` at a vertex (coefficient on 𝟏).\nFrom the Hecke relation σ⁻¹ = σ - (q - q⁻¹):\n- pp: 0\n- nn: −(q − q⁻¹) = −HA\n- pn: −(q − q⁻¹)  (DOUBLED: actual is −HA/2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.w_plus_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.w_plus_t","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L81-L90","doc":"The crossing amplitude `𝔴⁺(q)` at a vertex (coefficient on σ).\nFrom the Hecke relation σ⁻¹ = σ - (q - q⁻¹):\n- pp: 1  (positive crossing = σ)\n- nn: 1  (negative crossing = σ⁻¹ = σ - HA)\n- pn: 1  (mixed = ½(σ + σ⁻¹), DOUBLED below to avoid ½) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vertexType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vertexType","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L75-L79","doc":"Determine vertex type from two nucleon types. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instInhabitedNucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instInhabitedNucleonType","kind":"instance","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instInhabitedNucleonType.default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instInhabitedNucleonType.default","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType","kind":"instance","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprNucleonType.repr","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqNucleonType","kind":"instance","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.neutron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.neutron","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType.proton","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NucleonType","kind":"inductive","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L69-L73","doc":"Nucleon type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprVertexType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprVertexType","kind":"instance","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instReprVertexType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instReprVertexType.repr","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqVertexType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.instDecidableEqVertexType","kind":"instance","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.pn","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.nn","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexType.pp","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.VertexType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.VertexType","kind":"inductive","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L62-L67","doc":"A vertex type: the crossing between two nucleons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HA_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HA_t","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L57-L58","doc":"Hecke amplitude over `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`: `HA = q − q⁻¹ = t² − t⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.s_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.s_skein","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The skein amplitude `s = t − t⁻¹ = q^{1/2} − q^{-1/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_from_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_from_t","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L51-L52","doc":"`q⁻¹ = t⁻²` in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L48-L49","doc":"`q = t²` in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t_inv","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L45-L46","doc":"`t⁻¹` (= q^{-1/2}) in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L42-L43","doc":"`t` (= q^{1/2}) in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.R_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.R_t","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrix.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Extended ground ring: `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]` where `t² = q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}